(4037189, 573116, 64795, '<td valign="top">I LOVED this one!!! Gave it an 8, and now seeing the end score, I wish I would have given a 10.  It is very artistic. Screw ''DNMC''.  How did you create this image?</td>', 'I LOVED this one!!! Gave it an 8, and now seeing the end score, I wish I would have given a 10.  It is very artistic. Screw ''DNMC''.  How did you create this image?', '2007-08-29 01:56:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(4037204, 575544, 60862, '<td valign="top">Wow, that''s beautiful! Congrats!</td>', 'Wow, that''s beautiful! Congrats!', '2007-08-29 01:59:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(4037208, 575544, 57570, '<td valign="top">u''ve shot this so well! congrats!</td>', 'u''ve shot this so well! congrats!', '2007-08-29 02:00:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(4037211, 575405, 60862, '<td valign="top">My eye goes right to the space between the trees.  It''s like their dancing or shaking hands.</td>', 'My eye goes right to the space between the trees.  It''s like their dancing or shaking hands.', '2007-08-29 02:01:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(4037217, 575469, 79720, '<td valign="top">Congrats. Nice to see the DPC agrees with me on this image.</td>', 'Congrats. Nice to see the DPC agrees with me on this image.', '2007-08-29 02:01:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(4037219, 574989, 78303, '<td valign="top">First of all, I was a little upset this got disqualified, as I know I just used basic editing, but I received a DQ because I downloaded it with Adobe PS Elements, adding a copyright line in the EXIF in the process.  FOr that reason, it was no longer an "original" and had to be tossed by the committee.  Oh well...I move on.<br/> <br/> In response to the comments below.<br/> <br/>1.  Silverscreen.  This was a single JPG image.  I thought you needed at least 3 images to do HDR?  I just, flat out, went overboard on the curves and shadows and contrast trying to make it cool.  I failed.<br/>2.  jblaylockrayner.  Noe, I just overdid basic editing.  I probably pushed the boundary of it a bit too far, but being a PP noob, I couldn''t stop myself.<br/>3.  kaarissaa.  Thank you for enjoying the picture.<br/>4.  annig, um...the backlighting would be the sunlight shining behind the flower.  I placed the flower directly over the afternoon sun.  BUt, my poor editing probably overshadowed that.<br/>5.  Larus, you hit it on the head - I went overboard when I should not have.  Thank you for the honest critique.<br/></td>', 'First of all, I was a little upset this got disqualified, as I know I just used basic editing, but I received a DQ because I downloaded it with Adobe PS Elements, adding a copyright line in the EXIF in the process.  FOr that reason, it was no longer an "original" and had to be tossed by the committee.  Oh well...I move on.  In response to the comments below. 1.  Silverscreen.  This was a single JPG image.  I thought you needed at least 3 images to do HDR?  I just, flat out, went overboard on the curves and shadows and contrast trying to make it cool.  I failed.2.  jblaylockrayner.  Noe, I just overdid basic editing.  I probably pushed the boundary of it a bit too far, but being a PP noob, I couldn''t stop myself.3.  kaarissaa.  Thank you for enjoying the picture.4.  annig, um...the backlighting would be the sunlight shining behind the flower.  I placed the flower directly over the afternoon sun.  BUt, my poor editing probably overshadowed that.5.  Larus, you hit it on the head - I went overboard when I should not have.  Thank you for the honest critique.', '2007-08-29 02:02:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(4037288, 575139, 60862, '<td valign="top">A delightful capture of summer. :)</td>', 'A delightful capture of summer. :)', '2007-08-29 02:24:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(4037295, 575249, 60862, '<td valign="top">Very nice composition, Rob!  I also like the colors.  Congrats on a new personal top 5!  My only issue is the bright blob on the leftmost pitcher. Were you using your on-camera flash?</td>', 'Very nice composition, Rob!  I also like the colors.  Congrats on a new personal top 5!  My only issue is the bright blob on the leftmost pitcher. Were you using your on-camera flash?', '2007-08-29 02:26:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(4037298, 575285, 60862, '<td valign="top">Pretty colors.  Would''ve fit nicely into the blur side challenge, as the blur encourages me to expore the colors and shapes more than worry about sharp edges.</td>', 'Pretty colors.  Would''ve fit nicely into the blur side challenge, as the blur encourages me to expore the colors and shapes more than worry about sharp edges.', '2007-08-29 02:26:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(4037302, 575377, 60862, '<td valign="top">So it''s a stained-glass window?  Something about it left me wondering.  Very pretty colors and textures, and I like the angled composition.<br/> <br/>Edited to add: Wow!  Look at that average from  your commenters.  You certainly found your audience! :)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-08-29 01:28:50.</i></td>', 'So it''s a stained-glass window?  Something about it left me wondering.  Very pretty colors and textures, and I like the angled composition. Edited to add: Wow!  Look at that average from  your commenters.  You certainly found your audience! :)', '2007-08-29 02:28:17.000000', '2007-08-29 02:28:50.000000', 0),
(4037311, 575471, 60862, '<td valign="top">My first thought was that the leaf in the lower right is extraneous and distracts from the grasshopper.  But now I''m thinking it balances the dark area in the upper left nicely.  Either way, the use of darks and lights directs my eye nicely to the grasshopper.</td>', 'My first thought was that the leaf in the lower right is extraneous and distracts from the grasshopper.  But now I''m thinking it balances the dark area in the upper left nicely.  Either way, the use of darks and lights directs my eye nicely to the grasshopper.', '2007-08-29 02:30:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(4037314, 575343, 60862, '<td valign="top">Ah, you got good stuff that day!  I think it''s a lovely shot, nicely sharp, with interesting textures and halo light around his head.  I think the composition hurt the score, though.  Dead center leaves my eye to wander around.  I wonder how it''d look cropped in on the right?</td>', 'Ah, you got good stuff that day!  I think it''s a lovely shot, nicely sharp, with interesting textures and halo light around his head.  I think the composition hurt the score, though.  Dead center leaves my eye to wander around.  I wonder how it''d look cropped in on the right?', '2007-08-29 02:31:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(4037319, 575300, 60862, '<td valign="top">Nice lighting.  I''d suggest cropping in a bit on the left, too.  But really, I''d be curious to know how this would look seriously out of focus.  That would push the viewer to admire the shapes, darks, and lights, without trying to see details that just aren''t there.</td>', 'Nice lighting.  I''d suggest cropping in a bit on the left, too.  But really, I''d be curious to know how this would look seriously out of focus.  That would push the viewer to admire the shapes, darks, and lights, without trying to see details that just aren''t there.', '2007-08-29 02:33:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(4037322, 572388, 60862, '<td valign="top">Oooooh.  Preeeetty! :)  I really like the addition of the water drops - adds a whole new dimension to the texture.<br/> <br/>Edited to add:  Congrats on your new personal best, too! :)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-08-29 01:34:56.</i></td>', 'Oooooh.  Preeeetty! :)  I really like the addition of the water drops - adds a whole new dimension to the texture. Edited to add:  Congrats on your new personal best, too! :)', '2007-08-29 02:34:03.000000', '2007-08-29 02:34:56.000000', 0),
(4037332, 575469, 57570, '<td valign="top">guys, I am absolutely thrilled!!! Thankyou everyone for your votes and comments.</td>', 'guys, I am absolutely thrilled!!! Thankyou everyone for your votes and comments.', '2007-08-29 02:42:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(4037339, 575377, 53316, '<td valign="top">I just adore the colors here. I love the simple composition as well.</td>', 'I just adore the colors here. I love the simple composition as well.', '2007-08-29 02:46:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(4037347, 575034, 64795, '<td valign="top">This is really nice!  The score is well-deserved.  Thanks for the comment too. :)</td>', 'This is really nice!  The score is well-deserved.  Thanks for the comment too. :)', '2007-08-29 02:51:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(4037359, 575300, 48228, '<td valign="top">I am a little surprised that this didn''t do better, as I love the play of light in this backlighting..</td>', 'I am a little surprised that this didn''t do better, as I love the play of light in this backlighting..', '2007-08-29 02:55:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(4037384, 573116, 54033, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by daboardergirl:</b></div><hr/><i> I LOVED this one!!! Gave it an 8, and now seeing the end score, I wish I would have given a 10.  It is very artistic. Screw ''DNMC''.  How did you create this image? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Loool.<br/>Its pretty much a straight out of the camera shot. I was about 600 feet away from the rider, and I was really trying to photograph the dust layers, which the horses stirred, being back light by the sun. So the order in the photograph goes like this (Sun then layers of dust then the rider then the last layer of dust that had received the darker shadow of the rider then 600 feet away the lens then me) Thanks. I love it too.<br/>Thanks, I love it too</td>', 'Originally posted by daboardergirl: I LOVED this one!!! Gave it an 8, and now seeing the end score, I wish I would have given a 10.  It is very artistic. Screw ''DNMC''.  How did you create this image?   Loool.Its pretty much a straight out of the camera shot. I was about 600 feet away from the rider, and I was really trying to photograph the dust layers, which the horses stirred, being back light by the sun. So the order in the photograph goes like this (Sun then layers of dust then the rider then the last layer of dust that had received the darker shadow of the rider then 600 feet away the lens then me) Thanks. I love it too.Thanks, I love it too', '2007-08-29 03:13:08.000000', NULL, 0),
